{"conversation_evidence":{"admissible_pre_tfg_turns":[{"create_time":1692624031.820827,"event_index":2,"role":"user","source_node_id":"aaa267d7-5c52-40e5-af86-12a8e5a72230","source_parent_id":"e0591b4a-a53a-4f51-a509-8899faf08748","source_record_index":2,"text":"The following query in Postgres:\n```\n\t\tDELETE FROM timeouts\n\t\tWHERE last_seen < $1\n\t\tRETURNING peer, game, lobbies\n\t\tLIMIT 1\n```\nReturns\n```\nsyntax error at or near \"LIMIT\" (SQLSTATE 42601)\n``\nHow do I fix this?","turn_id":"turn_000002"}],"first_generation":{"artifacts":[{"candidate_id":"GTC_000003_000425_000769_c65f9dbda438eb9b","completeness":"complete","container":"markdown_fence","continuation_status":"none","detector":{"name":"generated-technical-content-v2","version":"2"},"detector_evidence":["complete_standalone_markdown_fence","statement_terminators"],"end_offset":769,"fence_language":"sql","kind":"source_code","legacy_artifact_id":"ARTIFACT_000003_001","order_within_response":1,"raw_text":"WITH deleted_rows AS (\n    SELECT peer, game, lobbies \n    FROM timeouts\n    WHERE last_seen < $1\n    LIMIT 1\n)\nDELETE FROM timeouts\nUSING deleted_rows\nWHERE timeouts.peer = deleted_rows.peer\nAND timeouts.game = deleted_rows.game\nAND timeouts.lobbies = deleted_rows.lobbies\nRETURNING deleted_rows.peer, deleted_rows.game, deleted_rows.lobbies;\n","raw_text_sha256":"c65f9dbda438eb9b922a5f24c9c780236366fb70c564f34892dbcb7541cecc02","source_event_index":3,"source_record_index":3,"source_response_id":"turn_000003","source_turn_text_sha256":"e042c112c3e39cae57d390418965d840de53150da6b6753ec35686876a47a02d","start_offset":425,"status":"candidate_requires_semantic_review"}],"identification":{"ambiguity_reason":"","artifact_refs":["GTC_000003_000425_000769_c65f9dbda438eb9b"],"boundary":"exclusive_before:turn_000003","candidate_artifact_ids":["GTC_000003_000425_000769_c65f9dbda438eb9b"],"family_id":"FGF_1e032351bf994e6f0381ecd6","family_id_provenance":{"algorithm":"sha256","canonical_input":{"artifact_ids":["GTC_000003_000425_000769_c65f9dbda438eb9b"],"case_id":"CASE_36ED555D6DE4"},"canonicalization":"json-sort-keys-compact-utf8","case_id_included":true,"digest_hex":"1e032351bf994e6f0381ecd61a5049f8dbfd58e090b57ed8a9be3a4addaf0304","digest_prefix_length":24},"family_label":"PostgreSQL CTE-based limited-row DELETE query","rationale":"The assistant’s first generated technical-content family is the SQL query using a CTE to select one matching row and delete it. The sole candidate is generated in turn_000003, directly triggered by the user’s request in turn_000002.","response_event_index":3,"response_turn_id":"turn_000003","status":"complete","target_prompt_event_index":2,"target_prompt_id":"turn_000002"}},"first_generation_response":{"create_time":1692624058.574449,"event_index":3,"role":"assistant","source_node_id":"a31056ed-50b7-49e4-8318-4bde0e8453eb","source_parent_id":"aaa267d7-5c52-40e5-af86-12a8e5a72230","source_record_index":3,"text":"The `DELETE` statement in PostgreSQL does not support a `LIMIT` clause directly. The error you're seeing is due to the presence of the `LIMIT 1` clause in your `DELETE` statement. \n\nTo delete a limited number of rows, you can use a Common Table Expression (CTE) with the `DELETE` statement. Here's a way you can modify your query to delete a single row (similar to using `LIMIT 1`) based on your provided conditions:\n\n```sql\nWITH deleted_rows AS (\n    SELECT peer, game, lobbies \n    FROM timeouts\n    WHERE last_seen < $1\n    LIMIT 1\n)\nDELETE FROM timeouts\nUSING deleted_rows\nWHERE timeouts.peer = deleted_rows.peer\nAND timeouts.game = deleted_rows.game\nAND timeouts.lobbies = deleted_rows.lobbies\nRETURNING deleted_rows.peer, deleted_rows.game, deleted_rows.lobbies;\n```\n\nThis CTE selects the first row matching your condition, then deletes only that row from the `timeouts` table. \n\nDo note that this approach can be less performant than a straightforward `DELETE` when working with large tables, but for small operations, the difference is often negligible. If you frequently find yourself needing to delete a small number of rows based on complex criteria, this method should be suitable.","turn_id":"turn_000003"},"target_developer_prompt":{"create_time":1692624031.820827,"event_index":2,"role":"user","source_node_id":"aaa267d7-5c52-40e5-af86-12a8e5a72230","source_parent_id":"e0591b4a-a53a-4f51-a509-8899faf08748","source_record_index":2,"text":"The following query in Postgres:\n```\n\t\tDELETE FROM timeouts\n\t\tWHERE last_seen < $1\n\t\tRETURNING peer, game, lobbies\n\t\tLIMIT 1\n```\nReturns\n```\nsyntax error at or near \"LIMIT\" (SQLSTATE 42601)\n``\nHow do I fix this?","turn_id":"turn_000002"}},"csv_extraction":{"context":[{"category":"context","evidence_spans":["DELETE FROM timeouts\n\t\tWHERE last_seen < $1\n\t\tRETURNING peer, game, lobbies\n\t\tLIMIT 1"],"item_id":"context_1","normalized_text":"A PostgreSQL DELETE statement targets rows in the `timeouts` table where `last_seen < $1`, returns `peer`, `game`, and `lobbies`, and appends `LIMIT 1`.","source_roles":["user"],"source_turn_ids":["turn_000002"]},{"category":"context","evidence_spans":["syntax error at or near \"LIMIT\" (SQLSTATE 42601)"],"item_id":"context_2","normalized_text":"PostgreSQL reports a syntax error at or near `LIMIT` with SQLSTATE 42601 for the supplied statement.","source_roles":["user"],"source_turn_ids":["turn_000002"]}],"specificity":[{"category":"specificity","evidence_spans":["How do I fix this?"],"item_id":"specificity_1","normalized_text":"The user wants the supplied PostgreSQL query fixed.","source_roles":["user"],"source_turn_ids":["turn_000002"]}],"verification":[]},"identity":{"case_id":"CASE_36ED555D6DE4","conversation_id":"7e23cfa9-7ae9-4d83-bf46-f4ee1f25465f","conversation_url":"https://chat.openai.com/share/7e23cfa9-7ae9-4d83-bf46-f4ee1f25465f","outcome_class":"PA","pr_conversation_correspondence":"yes","pr_number":50,"pr_url":"https://github.com/poki/netlib/pull/50","repositor